WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.488
Good morning, it's Friday, November 13.

00:00:02.552 --> 00:00:09.251
This is Signal in the AI Fog, your daily briefing on enterprise AI in production, written and read by AI.

00:00:09.315 --> 00:00:18.247
Today: Inference pricing becomes a menu of tiers, Gemini 2.5 traffic reroutes on December first, and AI Act marking arrives December second.

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:20.097
First, the story of the day.

00:00:20.161 --> 00:00:23.606
Anthropic released Claude Fable 5.2 on November ninth.

00:00:23.670 --> 00:00:30.496
Its documentation lists eight dollars per million input tokens and forty dollars per million output tokens.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.366
It requires thirty-day data retention unless Anthropic expressly authorizes zero retention.

00:00:36.429 --> 00:00:48.870
According to Resultsense, an optional fast mode runs up to two and a half times quicker at double the price: sixteen dollars per million input tokens and eighty dollars per million output tokens.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:56.654
Meta's Muse Ember, aimed at repetitive agent work, costs ten cents per million input tokens, according to press coverage.

00:00:56.718 --> 00:01:07.691
Google opened Gemini 4 Carbon to all paying developers on November tenth, at an introductory two dollars per million input tokens and ten dollars per million output tokens.

00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:12.540
Press reports put the end of that introductory price at November thirtieth.

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:17.817
The bigger picture: a price per token no longer describes a route.

00:01:17.888 --> 00:01:26.250
Look at what varied in a single week: speed tier, retention terms, model size, and an expiry date on the price itself.

00:01:26.321 --> 00:01:31.990
For a platform team, a route now needs more fields than a model name and a rate.

00:01:32.061 --> 00:01:38.438
Add latency tier, retention class and price-valid-until, and let gateway policy read them.

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:40.493
Budget each tier separately.

00:01:40.564 --> 00:01:43.824
Put the November thirtieth expiry in an alert.

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:49.422
Test cheap executor models on your own evaluation set before they take volume.

00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:58.280
Likely consequence: the cheapest sensible route changes monthly, so routing becomes a regular review, not a one-time design.

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:00.619
Next, Models and vendors.

00:02:00.688 --> 00:02:08.687
According to migration guides, Google deprecated Gemini 2.5 Pro and 2.5 Flash in the Gemini API on November second.

00:02:08.757 --> 00:02:17.521
From December first, requests are routed automatically to Gemini 3.8 Flash and Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite, at those models' prices.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:21.346
Several audio previews shut down November seventeenth.

00:02:21.416 --> 00:02:25.450
Gemini 3.6 Flash retires on Vertex on November nineteenth.

00:02:26.050 --> 00:02:33.462
Why it matters: an automatic reroute keeps your integration answering, but with a different model and a different bill.

00:02:33.524 --> 00:02:44.050
Pin the successor now, run your evaluation set against it before December first, and check that your gateway flags silent model substitutions rather than absorbing them.

00:02:44.650 --> 00:02:45.726
Next, Platform.

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:59.210
MuleSoft says its Omni Gateway now supports more than 140 models from vendors including OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Mistral, xAI and NVIDIA, plus models hosted on Amazon Bedrock and Azure.

00:02:59.281 --> 00:03:04.732
Each model inherits existing authentication, rate limits and audit policies.

00:03:04.804 --> 00:03:09.322
An in-house or sovereign model can be registered as a provider.

00:03:09.394 --> 00:03:12.550
The gateway is included in the subscription.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:19.318
What this really signals: API management vendors are converging with AI gateways.

00:03:19.394 --> 00:03:23.277
Inheritance is convenient, but it is also the risk.

00:03:23.353 --> 00:03:32.033
A fast tier or a decision-style endpoint should not silently inherit its parent model's quota or retention policy.

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.470
Ask how your gateway treats it.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.268
Next, Regulation.

00:03:36.338 --> 00:03:41.553
The Digital Omnibus on AI entered into force on July twenty-seventh, 2026.

00:03:41.623 --> 00:03:53.885
According to Mayer Brown, watermarking obligations for AI-generated content apply from December second, 2026, earlier than the February 2027 date the Commission had proposed.

00:03:53.955 --> 00:04:03.750
Per Loyens and Loeff, stand-alone high-risk systems follow on December second, 2027, and embedded safety components on August second, 2028.

00:04:04.350 --> 00:04:10.081
Reading between the lines: the marking date stayed close while high-risk duties slipped.

00:04:10.146 --> 00:04:14.054
That makes December second the nearest hard AI Act deadline.

00:04:14.119 --> 00:04:15.487
Nineteen days remain.

00:04:15.552 --> 00:04:24.670
Inventory which of your generative pipelines produce text, images or audio, and check whether your vendors or your own code mark the output.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:26.047
A follow-up.

00:04:26.112 --> 00:04:33.363
Expected: Anthropic's pricing on November eighteenth and first trade on November nineteenth, then only reported.

00:04:33.428 --> 00:04:36.406
Anthropic has now announced both dates itself.

00:04:36.471 --> 00:04:37.895
The number of the day.

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.061
Double the price.

00:04:39.126 --> 00:04:48.837
That is what Claude Fable 5.2's optional fast mode costs: sixteen dollars per million input tokens, for a response up to two and a half times quicker.

00:04:48.902 --> 00:04:49.808
What to watch.

00:04:49.873 --> 00:04:51.103
Next week is dense.

00:04:51.168 --> 00:04:59.326
Microsoft Ignite and Google's Sovereign AI Summit start November seventeenth, the day several Gemini audio previews shut down.

00:04:59.391 --> 00:05:04.311
Anthropic prices its IPO November eighteenth and trades November nineteenth.

00:05:04.376 --> 00:05:09.426
OVHcloud's summit and Gemini 3.6 Flash retirement also fall on the nineteenth.

00:05:09.491 --> 00:05:13.441
Walmart's Agent Profiles are due about November twenty-first.

00:05:13.505 --> 00:05:25.354
Then Carbon's introductory price ends November thirtieth, Gemini 2.5 requests reroute December first, AI Act marking starts December second, and EuroHPC's Lot 2 closes December third.

00:05:25.418 --> 00:05:27.296
And a question for your team.

00:05:27.361 --> 00:05:35.389
Which fields does a route in your gateway carry besides model name and price: speed tier, data retention, price expiry date?

00:05:35.454 --> 00:05:38.173
Who gets alerted when one of them changes?

00:05:38.238 --> 00:05:39.533
That's it for today.

00:05:39.598 --> 00:05:42.123
Sources are in the episode description.

00:05:42.187 --> 00:05:44.130
This was Signal in the AI Fog.

00:05:44.195 --> 00:05:45.360
See you on Monday.
